  "body": "Slice 2a of #4081 (the laser profile cut): the generator in the motion crate. The app operation is slice 2b. This PR does not depend on slice 1 (#4270).\n\n## What changed\n\n- **The waterjet generator speaks with a voice from its params.** `WaterjetParams` gets `voice: Voice`. The about 20 hard-coded \"waterjet profile\" / \"waterjet:\" texts in `motion::waterjet` (door, planner, tabs, emitter, notes) now read `p.voice`. `sheet::Voice` gets a `short` word for the notes (`plasma`, `wire`, `waterjet`, `laser`) and a new `Voice::LASER` (\"laser profile\", tool \"beam\").\n- **Every waterjet sentence is the same as before.** The pierce note keeps its abrasive text under the waterjet voice. Under another voice it names the voice's tool (\"beam and dwell records are not implemented\").\n- **New `motion::laser`**: `LaserParams` (the waterjet's numbers without the abrasive delay, plus `power`) and `laser_profile`. It checks the power by name (more than 0, at most 100 % of the source's maximum), converts to `WaterjetParams` with `Voice::LASER`, and runs the same planner, tabs, emitter, kerf law and cover law. A note states the requested power. No CL record carries the power yet (slice 3, the laser post).\n- Callers: `crates/app/src/operation/waterjet_op.rs` and the waterjet golden test set `voice: Voice::WATERJET`.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/4081-laser-motion.md`. It says why the laser rides the waterjet generator (the same sheet rules; no copy of about 500 lines) and why the power is a percent (the Grbl laser mode scales S against `$30`).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`camcraft-motion` lib, `laser::tests`:\n- `the_laser_cuts_what_the_waterjet_cuts_and_speaks_as_the_laser`: the same moves as the waterjet for the same numbers. Every note starts with `laser: `, and no note names the abrasive or the jet.\n- `the_power_is_refused_by_name_outside_its_range`: 0, -5, 100.5 and NaN are refused. 100 is legal.\n- `the_shared_refusals_speak_as_the_laser_profile`: the kerf, clearance, tab count, tab position and empty input refusals say \"laser profile:\".\n- `an_open_run_and_a_missing_silhouette_say_so_in_the_lasers_words`.\n\nThe waterjet stays pinned by its unchanged tests: `waterjet::tests` (11), `waterjet_profile` (8), `mcp_waterjet`, and the golden `waterjet_tabbed_plate_with_holes.cl` (no change).\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 14 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --lib -- waterjet plasma wire_edm sheet laser`: 138 passed.\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-motion -- -D warnings` and `-p camcraft-app`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Heavy lanes: **not run**. `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` reaches every motion and app heavy target (115 steps), because `motion` and `waterjet_op.rs` changed. The change does not alter any path: the waterjet golden and the moves-equality test show this. The heavy run is owed before the PR is flagged ready.\n- No app operation, no UI and no post for the laser yet.\n\nChangelog: none (no user-visible change until slice 2b adds the Laser Profile operation).\n\nRefs #4081\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
